{"ts":"2026-09-08T05:49:58.852Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"22d7da348d66bb9f892a835e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-bukwmy","claim:pm-doxj","claim:pm-e9zh","claim:pm-g8t7b9","claim:pm-lnrk","claim:pm-pd7nh0","claim:pm-qnl2","claim:pm-wg07","lineage:pm-g8t7b9","lineage:pm-4k6b","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-bukwmy+pm-doxj+pm-e9zh+pm-g8t7b9+pm-lnrk+pm-pd7nh0+pm-qnl2+pm-wg07","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-bukwmy","claim:pm-doxj","claim:pm-e9zh","claim:pm-g8t7b9","claim:pm-lnrk","claim:pm-pd7nh0","claim:pm-qnl2","claim:pm-wg07","lineage:pm-g8t7b9","lineage:pm-4k6b","lineage:pm-9rxu","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Proposal and provenance\n\nStable algorithm slug: `hash-keyed-summary-pyramid`. Source: pm-4k6b note recorded 2026-07-25T12:33:12.348Z.\n\nPlanning pass 2026-07-25 (directed maintainer pass): Algorithm (21) hash-keyed hierarchical summary pyramid — (9) chooses a coarse or fine representation of a candidate at read time, but at a million items the coarse representation of a large subtree must already exist, because summarizing an epic with four thousand descendants inside a sub-second read is not possible. Mechanism: maintain a summary per interior node of the parent hierarchy, keyed by a hash over the subtree's material state (child ids, their status, their updated versions). A read serves the stored summary when the key matches and marks it stale otherwise; refresh is incremental and bottom-up, touching only nodes whose subtree hash changed, which is the same fold shape as (6) write-time signal maintenance and should share its machinery. The pyramid gives the packer a genuine dial: represent a whole subtree in one summary row when the budget is tight, descend when it is not, with cost proportional to the depth served rather than the subtree size. Two properties must hold: a stale summary is always labelled rather than silently served, and the summary is derivable — losing the entire pyramid degrades performance and never correctness. Relation: write-side complement to (9); consumer of (6); the natural storage owner is the persistent derived index (pm-801d) rather than a separate artifact, and it should be filed there if the ADR accepts it.\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nEvaluate this mechanism as a bounded public-SDK experiment before any production adoption. Use the existing scorer and packer contracts; no CLI-only behavior or new command noun. The historical catalog is design input, not evidence that this mechanism was implemented.\n\n## Experiment protocol\n\nFreeze a workspace/history revision and parameter manifest. Compare against the current deterministic SDK baseline using held-out judgments and negative controls. Report nDCG/action success, critical-evidence omission, latency p50/p95, peak memory, tokens per completed task, and rebuild cost separately. Include 3-item/minutes, real-shaped, 100k/1M-item, decades-long, and sparse/dense/imbalanced graph scenarios; smoke subsets may not claim scale acceptance. Bound candidate counts, graph expansions, elapsed time, and output size, with cancellation and completeness receipts. Record exact versus approximate behavior and approximation error; theoretical guarantees require their stated assumptions. Missing or untrusted evidence remains unknown, never inferred proof.\n\nPromotion requires a reproducible quality improvement on the held-out target population, no regression of existing exact invariants or mandatory gates, and a declared compute/token cost justified by that improvement. Reject or defer with the same immutable evidence if those conditions fail. No production default, adaptive learning, or data export is authorized by this planning item."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-7go3ml"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Experiment: hash keyed summary pyramid"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Evaluate this mechanism as a bounded public-SDK experiment before any production adoption. Use the existing scorer and packer contracts; no CLI-only behavior or new command noun. The historical catalog is design input, not evidence that this mechanism was implemented. Distinct objective: hash keyed summary pyramid."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"draft"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["algorithm-proposal","hash-keyed-summary-pyramid","horizon-exploratory"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-08T05:49:58.852Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-08T05:49:58.852Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":480},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Define a versioned public-SDK input/output and parameter contract, with exact source receipts and bounded time, memory and token complexity.; Implement an isolated reproducible prototype and compare held-out quality, task success, costs, cold-start behavior and negative controls against the unchanged baseline.; Record an accept, reject, or defer decision with evidence; production implementation requires an accepted decision and its own linked delivery scope."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-4k6b"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A falsifiable decision on hash keyed summary pyramid with reusable benchmark evidence and no unreviewed production policy change."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-g8t7b9","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-08T05:49:58.852Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-vvib","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-09-08T05:49:58.852Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-08T05:49:58.852Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: complete all-status 2658-item title/metadata catalog and source ledger reviewed; current query hash keyed summary pyramid nearest pm-2qahia,pm-aka8m7,pm-4k6b,pm-79gv6q,pm-mg13iz. No individual owner for this experiment was found. Shared scorer/signal/packer baselines are prerequisites, not proof of this distinct mechanism. User requested individual planning records; this draft preserves the open cognitive-architecture decision gate and does not accept the ADR. Estimate is a one-day initial spike budget, not a delivery forecast."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2efc3b2b9a16d7d6eccf640ff109564a1ca46363e74b8d713f132f3e8a888e26","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f0c65923e1a4c947b7af18cbef494f6d3bacdaf69e98af998561e456ad29abce"}
